    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0932e1ba_f74bc712",
        "filename": "bp2build/metrics.go",
        "patchSetId": 48
      },
      "lineNbr": 69,
      "author": {
        "id": 1887575
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-13T18:11:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not in the instances we have here, but `alertFmt` can be an arbitrary formatting string, so one may not necessarily pass in just strings. More proximally, because of the way that Go handles varargs, `Fprintf` cannot cope with `fmt, cwd, vals...`, as it wants just `io.Writer, string, ...interface{}`. Further, Go won\u0027t accept e.g. `fmt, cwd, vals..., err.Error()`, which is bad because even if Go actually patterned varargs, the `err`\u0027s `%s` would have to go ahead of the `alertFmt`, thus the user experience could be a dump of a large error, then the intended human context below, vs. it introducing the error immediately, offering context.",
      "parentUuid": "7ae9bfed_662af853",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 69,
        "startChar": 46,
        "endLine": 69,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "51e01d46f282f5707a0d09045ed4688fa39bf874",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7fc0a569_e66fa269",
        "filename": "bp2build/metrics.go",
        "patchSetId": 48
      },
      "lineNbr": 69,
      "author": {
        "id": 1687194
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-13T20:42:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We don\u0027t need to change this right now, but in general, it\u0027s good to think about what level of flexibility is necessary now, not what might be used in the future ( go/yagni , https://testing.googleblog.com/2017/08/code-health-eliminate-yagni-smells.html).\n\nFor the code we have _right now_, each of these is only called with a single string: vals doesn\u0027t need to be able to handle varargs interface{} arguments, a single string would be sufficient.\n\nBlueprint/Soong already have functionality used widely for general error handling (e.g. ctx.Errorf/ctx.ModuleErrorf) and go has panic, so we\u0027re not likely to be extending use of this function.",
      "parentUuid": "0932e1ba_f74bc712",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 69,
        "startChar": 46,
        "endLine": 69,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "51e01d46f282f5707a0d09045ed4688fa39bf874",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
